<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8922" root="حلك" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَالِكٌ</span></b>  <i>Intensely black;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحْلَوْلِكٌ</span></b>  (K)
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُلَكْلِكٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُلْكُوكٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَلَكُوكٌ</span></b>  and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُحْلَنْكِكٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْتَحْلِكٌ</span></b>  (Ibn-'Abbád, K) and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُلَكَةٌ</span></b> . (TA.) You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْوَدُ حَالِكٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَانِكٌ</span>;
both meaning the same; (S;) i. e. <i>Black that is
intensely black.</i> (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حنك</span>.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّهُ</span>
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَحُلَكَةٌ</span></b>  <i>Verily he,</i> or <i>it, is intensely black.</i> (TA.)

